 ## 2026-09-11
 
+### 1620 — Pi context_window And model-harness --max-kv-size Are Now Bound Together
+- ROOT CAUSE: The deployed `qwen-3.8-27b-mlx-8bit` Pi profile (`context_window = 75000`) and the `qwen-local` model-harness profile it launches through `runtime.argv = ["run", "qwen-local", "--config", ...]` live in two separately edited files with no cross-check; `qwen-local` ran with no `--max-kv-size` at all until an operator hand-patched it on 2026-08-30. A `--max-kv-size` below `context_window` does not refuse — the runtime's active-generation KV cache is a fixed-size ring that silently overwrites the oldest tokens, so the failure mode is degraded output, not a loud error.
+- FIX: `validatePiModelHarnessKVBound` (`tools/agents-infra/internal/infra/pi_kv_bound.go`) runs inside `parsePiProfile`, the production project-config entry point. For a Pi runtime invoking `model-harness run PROFILE [--config PATH] ...`, it resolves the referenced model-harness profile via `modelharness.Resolve` (no process/socket side effects, matching `--print-config`'s static-resolution contract) and refuses when `--max-kv-size` is absent or below `context_window`, naming both values.
+- SCOPE excluded: profiles whose runtime is not `model-harness`, and `mode = "ssh"` model-harness profiles (the KV bound lives on the remote host argv, which a local config parse cannot observe).
+- GATE: `TestPiProfileRefusesContextWindowAboveModelHarnessKVBoundAtProductionEntry` covers absent bound and below-bound (including an exact off-by-one case that catches a `bound+1 < contextWindow` mutant a wider gap would miss); `TestPiProfileAdmitsContextWindowAtOrBelowModelHarnessKVBoundAtProductionEntry` proves the exact-equal and the deployed 75000/76800 pair are admitted; `TestPiProfileModelHarnessKVBoundIgnoresNonModelHarnessRuntimes` is the negative control for the executable-name gate. Deleting the guard call turns both refusal subtests red.
+- SCOPE: TASK-260830-heguyf (STORY-260830-i540ax); documented in `SKILL.md` and `README.md` next to the existing `model-harness stress`/context-window operator guidance. `context_window` values and other profile settings are unchanged; the deployed `/Users/alexis/src/.agents/.configs/model-harness.toml` and `project-config.toml` were read only, not modified, in this task.
+
 ### 1345 — Environment Admission Has a Coincidental Second Gate
 - FINDING: `validateProjectTarget` (tools/agents-infra/internal/infra/project_config.go) now refuses an unadmitted `environment` value through `ValidateLaunchableEnvironment` (agents_management_registry.go, TASK-260911-39bag5), but a downstream vendor/environment pairing `switch`'s `default` arm ALSO refuses any pair it does not explicitly admit — with a different message (`"vendor/environment pair %s/%s is not admitted"` vs `"must be one of codex, claude-code, pi"`). A mutant that let an unadmitted environment (e.g. a registered-but-unlaunchable agentic system such as `gemini-cli`) past the first gate was still coincidentally caught by the second when driven with a made-up vendor/environment pair, so a test asserting only `err != nil` at that call site passed against the mutant for the wrong reason.
 - FIX: `TestValidateProjectTargetRefusesRegisteredButUnlaunchableEnvironmentAtTheRealCallSite` asserts the specific gate's own wording, not mere error presence, to prove which gate actually refused.
